From 4f3cff8c0021c5fca096d1685d532abf5a3c91b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:27:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a worker's card filed across board files reaches
 its creator's human chat [daveey]

#544 walks creator_task_id -> parents on the card's own board file, so two cross-board shapes left hub
cards creator_chats_unresolved (t_01a19864fc42f5b2, t_01a1991923cadf9b):

- Worker node: a MacBook card leased to the hub runs there and its worker files a card on the hub's live
  board; the creator chain lives only in the board replica (sync-shadow/<board>.db). inherit_chats (and
  so the reconcile backfill) now falls back to resolve_chats on the replica, writes the created link and a
  notify sub whose cursor is the card's latest event (no replay).
- Placement: kanban_create routing a worker's card to another gateway (now, or deferred until its parents
  finish) sends the nearest real chat on this gateway that resolve_chats finds as the origin, never the
  worker transcript; unresolved -> no origin.

The CLI create never places remotely; its worker-node path is covered by the replica test.
